Job Description

This is a high-impact commercial legal role supporting the Wise Platform business that powers international payments for banks, financial institutions and enterprise partners around the world. Enterprise partners range from large regulated banks to embedded-payments and technology providers.

Your mission is to enable, protect and empower Wise Platform, providing first-rate commercial legal advice while improving and applying processes, templates and ways of working that let Legal scale in a rapidly-growing, fast paced environment. You'll be a trusted partner to Business Development, Product, Pricing and Compliance, bringing structure and predictability to how deals are run and the judgement to move quickly where it matters most.

To achieve this, you'll be:
• Part of the core team of lawyers owning all aspects of the contract lifecycle with bank partners, online platforms and enterprise customers;
• Building and embedding a process as well establish clear guardrails and expectations for when and how Legal engages;
• Applying a prioritisation framework to allocate legal resource appropriately;
• Owning template and playbook management, including annual reviews and clear communication on template updates;
• Driving effective communication and change management;
• Drafting, reviewing and negotiating agreements across a wide range of legal matters and ad hoc issues, including financial regulation, payments, banking and partnerships;
• Working closely with Product, Product Compliance and Pricing to ensure agreements reflect approved positions;
• Identifying and implementing tooling and technology solutions that streamline workflows and increase scalability;
• Understanding the real risks to the business and advising on the operational impact and practicalities of those risks; and
• Mentoring and upskilling other members of the Legal team and the wider business, making life simple and easy.

We are looking for a Payment Operations Specialist to join our Global Processing team to help our customers receive their funds faster globally. 

The role is a unique opportunity to join one of the fastest growing companies in Europe and help millions more potential customers save money by using Wise. 

Payment Operations Specialists play a crucial role in supporting the Payment Operations Organization reach its vision - seamless flow of customer funds. By ensuring high level execution of the daily responsibilities and consistently supporting Payment Operations in reaching the SLA’s, Payment Operations Specialists help our customers receive their funds faster 24/7 globally. The role gives a unique opportunity to learn how different currencies function, and impact customers on a global scale. 

The core ownership lies within daily tasks and responsibilities and the impact is well-defined, clear and largely shared collectively with the team. In this role, you'll add to that mission by:
• Maintaining consistent and high-level execution of daily tasks related to payment processing;
• Supporting your team by reaching your role set SLAs and KPIs which in turn contribute to the team by meeting team's main performance metrics and SLAs;
• Detecting and escalating domain-related problems and complex issues to Regional Payment Operations teams, ensuring timely and relevant communication with stakeholders;
• Following operational procedures and keeping track of critical updates.

We are looking for a candidate ready to leverage their Global regulatory experience in a dynamic, fintech environment. This is an exciting, hands-on opportunity working directly with our world-class Marketing organisation to launch compliant financial promotions. 



Your mission: 

Wise has already pioneered new ways for people to transfer money across borders and currencies. Our customers can also manage their hard-earned money with the World’s first platform to offer true international multi-currency accounts. Your mission is to enable our global marketing and product teams to launch new campaigns and manage our risk profile through a deep understanding of the regulatory requirements and Regulator’s expectations around them. 

Here’s how you’ll be contributing to the Global Product Compliance & Risk team, in the first line: 

Collaborate on Marketing Campaigns:
• Empower Marketing & Product Teams to launch risk based, brand forward promotional campaigns across all channels;
• Collaborate to design and implement a practical and comprehensive financial promotions framework;
• Perform pre-launch and ongoing marketing compliance legal and regulatory analysis and risk assessments; and
• Design scalable and customer-centric solutions to regulatory requirements;
• Offer effective advice to Marketing and Product Managers on existing and forthcoming Regulations, gaps, and risks. 

Manage and Mitigate Regulatory Risks and the Control Environment:
• As part of the Global Regulatory Product Compliance Team, you will identify and manage Regulatory Risks across all financial promotions offered to and for customers globally;
• Oversee the global control environment, designing effective, creative and targeted controls and evaluating the residual risk exposure;
• Collaborate with Compliance colleagues, to ensure Wise Product Teams are constantly aware of the most recent regulations and guidance; and
• Work with Marketing & Product Teams and the wider Risk & Compliance Team to implement and maintain Management Information that enables Wise to make informed decisions at the regional and Global levels. 

Audit, issue management and remediation:
• Conduct audit management and, where required, challenge audit findings in collaboration with Compliance second line and Product teams;
• Develop and deliver effective issue management to mitigate regulatory risks;

This role will give you the opportunity to:
• Grow your hands-on Fintech knowledge at full speed;
• Keep compliance right at the heart of the marketing lifecycle, in a fast-moving environment;
• Be empowered to identify ‘regulatory problems’ and take a lead in the solution design and implementation;

About you:
• You have previous experience of approving financial promotions/advertising gained either as part of a Compliance or Marketing role
• You have Financial Regulation advisory experience and are comfortable interpreting regulations (e.g. ASA requirements, COBS, UDAAP);
• Ability to analyze and interpret complex regulatory frameworks and apply them effectively;
• Ability to effectively communicate with Marketing Managers and Compliance and provide practical, actionable, and value added recommendations;
• Problem solving attitude, with the ability to use regulations together with data to drive business decisions;
• Experience (or interest) in working in a fast-growing environment and working directly with product teams;
• Willing to travel, as Wise offices are located across different countries; and
• Legally authorized to work in the UK 

Some extra skills that would be great:
• Experience working with marketing or product governance frameworks
• Experience with Confluence, Jira, Risk and Controls software
• Experience working with global teams

We’re looking for a passionate and people-centric Workplace Adviser to join our growing Workplace team. Based at our Tokyo office, you will help us to support day-to-day operations to foster a great workplace experience for our Wisers in Tokyo. 

Your mission:

Our Global Workplace Team plays a key part in the employee experience at Wise, through our curated spaces, events and services. Our mission is to create and maintain a safe and inspiring workplace for Wisers to achieve our Mission. As a workplace specialist, you are building your expertise in your field and starting to apply it to different types of problems proactively. The solutions you propose require weighing up a variety of factors before coming to a conclusion. Some of the tasks include:
• Ensuring our physical space is fully operational and processes are running efficiently, taking into consideration various factors and developing your expertise to handle different types of problems with minimal supervision;
• Developing a comprehensive understanding of the broader functions and goals of the company, aligning your expertise with the organisation's strategic objectives;
• Developing a network outside of your immediate team and build productive internal working relationships to collaboratively resolve mutual problems to enhance workplace efficiency;
• Actively building productive internal working relationships and act as a liaison between Wisers and the Workplace Team, gathering feedback and insights to continuously improve the workplace experience. Implement feedback mechanisms and surveys to gauge employee satisfaction and identify areas for enhancement, utilising moderate judgement to adapt processes when needed;
• Understanding and working within budget constraints, emphasising the importance of fiscal responsibility in all workplace projects and initiatives to support Mission Zero;
• Supporting the Workplace Leads and Project Managers with any ad-hoc projects, and take on more responsibility for local supervisory tasks when needed, assisting with medium-sized/complex issues and clients;
• Continuously building your expertise in workplace solutions and apply it to resolve a variety of routine and some complex issues within the company. Taking ownership of smaller, complex end-to-end projects that have a wider impact across the organization.;
• Ensure full site compliance with the Japanese Industrial Safety and Health Act (ISHA) and the local Labor Standards Inspection Office.
• Convene and lead the mandatory statutory Health and Safety Committee on a monthly basis.
• Manage the relationship and monthly consultations with the appointed Occupational Physician to review workplace risks, overtime fatigue, and associate wellbeing
• Coordinate and oversee the mandatory Annual Health Examinations for all local employees.
• Administer the statutory annual Stress Check Program, ensuring data privacy and facilitating follow-up physician consultations for high-stress individuals.
• Conduct routine workplace safety inspections to identify and mitigate physical hazards

As a financial institution moving billions of pounds of customer money in more than 70 countries, Wise must have bulletproof financials. We are now looking for a Cash Controller to join our Finance Team in London. This role is a unique opportunity to have an impact on Wise’s mission by ensuring timely and accurate financial data as well as building mature processes and a scalable control environment. 

A bit

about

the role:

As a Cash Controller you will be supporting the Balance Sheet Controller overseeing Wise’s financials, ensuring that Wise’s Cash balances across entities are controlled and reported accurately. Specific responsibilities include:
• Execute month end controls for cash balances across regions and entities ensuring balances are recorded accurately based on cut-off policies;
• Support the Balance Sheet controller in developing a robust substantiation program for cash balances with particular emphasis on financial statement assertions;
• Conduct periodic reviews of bank integrations ensuring adherence to policies, escalate exceptions to engineering teams so the root cause can be identified and fixed at source;
• Work closely with our first line BAAM controlling teams to provide guidance and support during bank account setup ensuring relevant reference data is captured and recorded appropriately;
• Develop a good understanding of bank account integrations to support external audit walkthroughs and documentation and acting as a first point of contact for Cash related questions;
• Create and maintain "end-to-end" documentation of how various transactions impact both Corporate and Customer Cash incorporating risk and controls;
• Identify missing or insufficient processes and take initiative to find solutions, in collaboration with other teams;
• Participate in team planning cycles and raise key items to remediate to make cash controlling more robust and secure;
• Build strong working relationships with the wider Finance Tribe.

